00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.960
a bloom filter is kind of like&nbsp;
a set in that you can add things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.440
to it and it quickly tells you&nbsp;
whether an element is in the set

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:02.160
except when you ask if an element is in the set it&nbsp;
either tells you "possibly yes" or "definitely no"

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.640
in other words if it tells you "no"&nbsp;
